
In this task, I designed a simple web infrastructure using a single server to host the website `www.foobar.com`. First, I created a diagram to illustrate the infrastructure and how its components communicate. Then, I explained the role of each component and the main issues with this architecture.

##  Infrastructure Design

![Simple Web Stack Diagram](0-simple_web_stack.png)

## Infrastructure Components

### 1. Server
A computer that provides services and resources to other computers over a network.

### 2. Domain Name
Provides an easy-to-remember address for accessing the website instead of using an IP address.

### 3. DNS Record
An **A record** maps `www.foobar.com` to the server's IPv4 address, `8.8.8.8`.

### 4. Web Server (Nginx)
Receives HTTP/HTTPS requests, serves static files, and forwards dynamic requests to the application server.

### 5. Application Server
Executes the application code and processes the website's business logic.

### 6. Database (MySQL)
Stores, retrieves, and manages the website's data.

### 7. Communication Protocol
The server communicates with the user's browser using HTTP or HTTPS over the internet.

## Infrastructure Issues

### 1. Single Point of Failure (SPOF)
If the only server fails, the entire website may become unavailable.

### 2. Downtime During Maintenance
Restarting services or deploying new code may temporarily interrupt the website.

### 3. Limited Scalability
A single server has limited resources and may become slow or unavailable when traffic increases significantly.

